    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "<!-- mintswarm: review round 2 -->\n### ✅ Review round 2: `pass`\n\npass: 0 blocker, 0 major, 0 minor, 0 nit (clear: nit, from the base config)\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- ✅ CODEOWNERS patterns match as GitHub's gitignore-style rules (F1 re-check) — *met*\n- ✅ Behaviour pinned by tests — *met*\n- ✅ Other criteria (approval groups, ownership model) — *met*\n\n<details><summary>Evidence and notes</summary>\n\n**Evidence per criterion**\n\n- **CODEOWNERS patterns match as GitHub's gitignore-style rules (F1 re-check)** (met): `Pattern::compile` in `crates/domain/src/codeowners.rs` now gates `rest.strip_prefix(\"**/\")` on `segment_start` (true at the start of the body and after a `/`). So `/x**/y` compiles to `x * * / y` and cannot cross a `/`. The trailing \"everything below\" meaning needs `core == \"**\" \\|\\| core.ends_with(\"/**\")`, so `/x**` behaves as `/x*`. Consecutive asterisks that are not a whole segment (`/a**b`, `***`) are plain stars, which is what gitignore says. A whole segment `**/` at the start or after a `/`, and a final `/**`, keep their meaning: `a/**/b` matches `a/b`, and `/**` matches `README.md` and `a/b/c.txt`.\n- **Behaviour pinned by tests** (met): New tests in `crates/domain/tests/codeowners.rs`: `double_star_inside_a_segment_is_plain_stars`, `a_trailing_double_star_inside_a_segment_owns_only_its_segment` and `an_anchored_bare_double_star_matches_everything`. `cargo test --offline -p mintswarm-domain --test codeowners` at the head gives `33 passed; 0 failed`.\n- **Other criteria (approval groups, ownership model)** (met (unchanged since round 1)): Commit 555876d touches only `crates/domain/src/codeowners.rs` (+6/-2) and `crates/domain/tests/codeowners.rs` (+27). No other lines differ from round 1.\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>Review stage, round 2 of #355 · [full review](https://github.com/mintswarm/mintswarm/issues/355/artifacts/9)</sub>",
